# Git guesses text-vs-binary by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8 KB, and
# a small PDF whose streams are not compressed contains none -- so git called
# projects/bpo-realtor/assets/forms/*.pdf TEXT and announced it would rewrite
# their line endings on the next checkout. That is silent corruption: the byte
# count changes, the xref offsets stop pointing at the right objects, and the
# file opens as a damaged PDF on somebody else's clone while looking perfect on
# the machine that committed it.
#
# Everything a project can legitimately commit and that is not source code is
# named here. Renders and footage stay gitignored; these are the small assets
# that ARE kept, for the reason in projects/bpo-realtor/project.json.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico    binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.wav   binary
*.m4a   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.onnx  binary

# Text that must keep LF regardless of platform: the ASS subtitle format and
# the shell scripts are read by tools that do not want CRLF.
*.ass   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
